  "reason": "Existing evidence shows that using imagenet_vit_l as the image encoder (config_039) achieves the highest accuracy so far (0.725). This experiment tests whether replacing the RNA encoder (scvi_n200 → pca_n2000) while keeping the image encoder, aggregation (transformer), and fusion (weighted) the same could maintain or improve accuracy. This clarifies the importance of RNA encoder choice with the already effective image encoder and fusion strategy. The expected cost is similar to config_039 (3.60 GPU hours), offering a low-cost exploration of a critical design choice."
}

